## Public interfaces

### `@slayzone/platform` — `SlayzoneDb`

```ts
import type { Database } from 'better-sqlite3'
export type SlayzoneDb = Database
```

Single-line type alias. Sustainability hedge: engine swap in slice 4+ = redefine alias in one file. No invented methods, no speculation on sync/async, no fake transaction shape. Concrete `Database` already satisfies; existing Electron IPC handlers untouched.

### `@slayzone/server` — programmatic API

```ts
export type StartServerConfig = {
  storeDir?: string   // defaults: SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR or ensureDataRoot()
  port?: number       // defaults: SLAYZONE_PORT, 0 = OS-assigned
  host?: string       // defaults: SLAYZONE_HOST or '127.0.0.1'
  mcpPort?: number    // reserved slice 3+, ignored this slice
  db?: SlayzoneDb     // pre-opened (tests); prod passes undefined
}

export type ServerHandle = {
  port: number
  host: string
  dataRoot: string
  healthCheck: () => Promise<boolean>
  stop: () => Promise<void>
}

export async function startServer(config?: StartServerConfig): Promise<ServerHandle>
```

CLI entry `bin.ts` reads env, calls `startServer()`, traps SIGTERM/SIGINT, idempotent shutdown.

