## Sustainability notes

1. **No structural DB interface this slice.** Type alias only. Designing `SlayzoneDatabase` shape w/o procedure consumers risks wrong abstraction (sync-only locks out async backends; bs3-flavored transaction shape misfits node:sqlite). Real abstraction designed from evidence in slice 4.
2. **Migrations stay in Electron main this slice.** Smallest behavior-preserving change. Move atomic w/ writer transition in slice ~8.
3. **`@slayzone/transport`'s in-process `ws-server.ts` deliberately not deleted this slice.** Kept to minimize diff. Delete in slice 4 when first procedure migrates + transport-server-as-host pattern fully phased out.
4. **Static guard catches `import 'electron'` in side-car-reachable code.** Future package additions to side-car deps need explicit allow-list entry in `check-server-electron-free.sh`.
